  "gaps": [
    "DEEPSEEK live ids as of 2026-09-27 are ONLY deepseek-flash (=V4.1-Flash, 2026-09-10) and deepseek-v4-pro (=V4-Pro-0813, 2026-08-13). deepseek-v4-flash and deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp are RETIRED (2026-09-10) but the ids still resolve and route to V4.1-Flash. models.dev lists them with release_date 2026-09-10 which is the RETIREMENT date, not a release.",
    "DEEPSEEK: V4-Pro is NOT retired. A 2026-09-14 redirect to V4.1-Flash was announced and then REVERSED. Any registry row marking v4-pro retired/deprecated is wrong.",
    "DEEPSEEK: DeepSeek-V4.1-Pro is named but NOT released (no id, no date, no repo). DeepSeek R2 and V5 have no official source.",
    "META BILLING: Muse Spark is PAYG per token, NOT subscription (Standard $1.25 in / $0.15 cached / $4.25 out). The Contributor tier is the ONLY training-opt-in tier ($0.10/$0.002/$0.20). No 1.1-contributor exists. There is NO 'muse-spark-1.0' id - the April model was announced unversioned.",
    "META: models.dev carries muse-spark-1.1 with release_date 2026-04-08 (the 1.0 announcement date) - importing verbatim would conflate the April and July models.",
    "XAI: grok-4.7 (live since 2026-09-21) is ABSENT from this deployment's xai provider list in ~/.hermes/config.yaml (lines 131-137 list grok-4.5, 4.3, 4.20-0309-*, 4.6, multi-agent, build-0.1). Same file's OpenRouter routing map (lines 973-976) omits x-ai/grok-4.6 and x-ai/grok-4.7. Line 993 routes 'router9/xai/grok-4', a slug retired 2026-05-15 that now silently redirects to grok-4.3.",
